MENDEL-GRUMAN CORPORATION


Mendel-Gruman Corporation is a futuristic transnational megacorporation that has fused scientific research, terraforming, and military might into a single entity. The company provided financial and military support to Roland Kane, and managed to create a fully terraformed biosphere on one lifeless planet. But behind these scientific achievements lay a far more sinister goal: using the local ecosystem and its inhabitants as the basis for creating biological weapons.

Mendel-Gruman's main strength is its military units—the MG soldiers, a well-equipped private army. Regular soldiers, veterans, snipers, and missilemen form the core of the force, while elite units use pulse rifles, flamethrowers, and heavy automatic weapons. Behind these combat units are the corporation's scientists, engaged in research and experimentation, transforming entire planetary complexes into closed scientific and military bases.

It was on this planet that Mendel-Gruman began studying the local subterranean insects. Scientists discovered that their organisms were capable of producing an extremely effective toxin that killed all living things nearby in seconds. The research quickly evolved into the development of biological weapons, and the planet's surface was transformed into a fortified network of complexes with defense systems, transport, and military garrisons.
